## Cohesion Check Complete: Zach-Bryan.md

**Before score: 9/10**
**After score: 9/10**

### Central Thesis

Zach Bryan is a Type 6 Loyalist: the fights, the records, and the apologies are one long search for something that deserves his devotion, which is why the most anti-machine figure in American music runs the biggest machine in American music.

### Thread Map

The chain holds end to end. The intro poses the paradox (anti-machine man, biggest machine) → the diagnosis section names the type and, notably, roadmaps the whole piece in its first paragraph ("three generations of Navy service... the discharge he openly resisted... an apology reflex") → childhood supplies the devotion origin (the Master Chief bottle) → the SEAL section shows the rupture that rerouted devotion into music → the machines section shows the trust inspections every institution fails → the apologies section shows the morning-after half of each fight → the sobriety section shows the private cost, bridged into faith via "Sobriety is the newest thing he trusts. The oldest is stranger" → the stadium section shows the one institution that passes inspection (the crowd) → "The other bottle" closes the frame the childhood section opened.

